Handle Edge Cases:
Edge Case Solutions:
Insufficient Funds:
Validate within transaction
Reject transfer/withdraw with clear error
Self-Transfer:
Disallow when fromAccountNumber == toAccountNumber
Negative/Zero Amount:
Reject request
Minimum transferable/depositable amount = 1 minor unit (e.g., 1 cent)
Closed/Suspended Wallet:
Block transfers, deposits, withdrawals
Allow statement retrieval only
Duplicate Client Requests (Retries):
Use client-provided idempotency key mapped to Transaction
Return prior result if request is repeated
Duplicate Payment Callbacks:
Ensure callback handler is idempotent
Update only if status changes from PENDING → COMPLETED/FAILED
Concurrency on Same Wallet:
Use distributed locks (STEP-7.5)
Use DB transaction for atomic balance updates
Rounding/Precision:
All balances stored in minor units (long)
No floating-point arithmetic
Large Amounts / Overflow:
Validate amount and balances do not overflow long
Define maximum allowed per transfer
Transfers to Non-Existent Wallet:
Validate destination wallet exists and is ACTIVE before debiting source
Statement Pagination:
Support pagination and time-window filtering
Prevents extremely large payloads
Notification Failures:
Log failures and retry asynchronously
Transaction commit is never blocked by notification issues
